{"qid":"Q1033","names":["Federal Republic of Nigeria"],"title":"Federal Republic of Nigeria","endonym":{"native":"Nijeriya","lang":"ha"},"capsule":"The Federal Republic of Nigeria emerged from British colonial rule as an independent state on 1 October 1960, becoming a republic within the Commonwealth in 1963. Despite severe disruption from the Biafran Civil War (1967–1970) and a succession of military coups between 1966 and 1999, Nigeria developed into Africa's most populous nation and largest economy, with Lagos as a continental financial hub and oil revenues from the Niger Delta funding the post-1970 state. A transition to civilian rule produced the Fourth Republic in 1999 under Olusegun Obasanjo, and Nigeria has maintained constitutional government since, though challenged by Boko Haram insurgency in the northeast from the 2000s onward.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Nigeria's borders are precisely defined by post-colonial international boundaries and are among the best-documented in Africa; internal administrative divisions and territorial control in conflict zones (Niger Delta, Lake Chad basin) are subject to ongoing qualification.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Nigeria","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Nigeria"}],"britannica":"place/Nigeria","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Nigeria","rulers":[{"qid":"Q335684","name":"Abubakar Tafawa Balewa","start":1960,"end":1966,"image":"Abubakar Tafawa Balewa (1962).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Abubakar%20Tafawa%20Balewa%20(1962).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"Abubakar","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q181782","name":"Nnamdi Azikiwe","start":1963,"end":1966,"image":"Dr. Nnamdi Azikiwe.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Dr.%20Nnamdi%20Azikiwe.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","artist":"FaridhaSL","attributionRequired":true}},{"qid":"Q354695","name":"Yakubu Gowon","start":1966,"end":1975,"image":"Gen. Yakubu Gowon GCFR (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Gen.%20Yakubu%20Gowon%20GCFR%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q379888","name":"Johnson Aguiyi-Ironsi","start":1966,"end":1966,"image":"Major Gen. J.T.U. Aguiyi Ironsi (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Major%20Gen.%20J.T.U.%20Aguiyi%20Ironsi%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q373628","name":"Murtala Muhammed","start":1975,"end":1976,"image":"Gen. Murtala Muhammed (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Gen.%20Murtala%20Muhammed%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Unknown authorUnknown author","attributionRequired":false},"nativeName":"Murtala Mohammed","nativeLang":"ha"},{"qid":"Q380668","name":"Shehu Shagari","start":1979,"end":1983,"image":"Shagaricropped.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Shagaricropped.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Public domain","artist":"Clawson","attributionRequired":false}},{"qid":"Q333415","name":"Ibrahim Babangida","start":1985,"end":1993,"image":"Ibrahim Babangida (cropped).jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Ibrahim%20Babangida%20(cropped).jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","artist":"Seiperi","attribution